In message <T6Jqd.18545$9A.303015@news.xtra.co.nz>, David Corbett wrote:
..
> On a related note, there are two entries on my player page (raven) from 
> other players who were "killed by a raven, while helpless".
> 
> I'm guessing the parser is just looking for the player's name followed 
> by a comma; in which case it should stop at the first comma. Or perhaps 
> a comma which doesn't have a space after it.

Teeny tiny bugs.  ;-)

Good guess on the cause; the script was doing:

	`/usr/bin/grep \" $username,\" $data_dir/scores.txt `

I changed that to:

	`/usr/bin/grep \" $username,\" $data_dir/scores.txt | grep -v \" $username, \"`

This _should_ work, since NetHack never puts a space after the comma following
the player name, but always puts a space before any additional death info (such
as ", while helpless").

-robin

